From ad4b7b2ff415711c285fcadfbe6a3e69d1311ded Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Gosman <andrei.gosman@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 11:35:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] support: provide cpu_set_t, sched_getcpu and
 sched_getaffinity on Darwin

cpu_set_t with its CPU_* helpers, sched_getcpu() and sched_getaffinity()
are glibc extensions. cpu_architecture_info.h exposes a cpu_set_t in its
public interface, bounded_object_pool.h and event_tracing.cpp pick a
segment or record the CPU with sched_getcpu(), and the CPU discovery in
cpu_architecture_info.cpp starts from sched_getaffinity(). None of them
compile on Darwin.

Add ocudu/support/os/sched_compat.h as a drop-in for <sched.h>. On Linux
it only includes <sched.h>. On Darwin it adds a cpu_set_t of the glibc
size with CPU_ZERO/SET/CLR/ISSET/COUNT, sched_getcpu() on top of
pthread_cpu_number_np() (macOS 11.0+), and a sched_getaffinity() that
reports every logical CPU from the hw.logicalcpu sysctl, because Darwin
has no per-thread affinity mask to read. The four users include the new
header instead of <sched.h>; their code is unchanged. On Darwin the CPU
topology discovery then sees all CPUs as allowed, no SMT sibling lists
and zero NUMA nodes, which is what the /sys readers also yield there.
---
 include/ocudu/support/cpu_architecture_info.h |  1 +
 .../support/memory_pool/bounded_object_pool.h |  2 +-
 include/ocudu/support/os/sched_compat.h       | 90 +++++++++++++++++++
 lib/support/cpu_architecture_info.cpp         |  1 +
 lib/support/tracing/event_tracing.cpp         |  2 +-
 5 files changed, 94 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 include/ocudu/support/os/sched_compat.h

